Metafold

A Whitepaper for the Pantheon

Version 0.1 – Draft

⸻

Abstract

Current approaches to intelligence—human and artificial—largely optimize navigation within existing conceptual spaces. Mathematics traverses manifolds. Optimization descends gradients. Language models search latent spaces.

Metafold proposes a complementary operation.

Rather than moving through an existing landscape, a Metafold reorganizes the landscape itself by changing the representation, ontology, or partition through which a problem is understood.

A Metafold is therefore an operator on conceptual spaces rather than an operator within them.

The Pantheon treats Metafold as a first-class semantic primitive.

⸻

Motivation

Many discoveries are not improvements within an existing model.

They arise because the model itself changes.

Examples include:

* heliocentric instead of geocentric astronomy
* calculus instead of geometric exhaustion
* relativity instead of absolute space and time
* information theory instead of communication by intuition
* object-oriented programming instead of procedural decomposition

These are not better paths.

They are different terrains.

Optimization alone cannot reliably discover them because optimization presumes the coordinate system.

Metafolds modify the coordinates.

⸻

Definition

Metafold

A transformation that changes the representation, ontology, coordinate system, or partition of a conceptual space while preserving or revealing higher-order invariants.

Unlike ordinary transformations, a Metafold acts upon the semantic geometry itself.

